{"uid":"12c71c6d9b992ac5","name":"test_docker_binary_is_genuinely_absent_from_the_constructed_path","fullName":"tests.test_status_docker_removed_from_path_task026#test_docker_binary_is_genuinely_absent_from_the_constructed_path","historyId":"bb1541975d95a072c83ccfd3f0c9ff3c","time":{"start":1791867587144,"stop":1791867587145,"duration":1},"description":"Precondition proof, isolated from the CLI: the helper this module\n    relies on for every other test here really does remove docker, using\n    this host's own ambient PATH (which does carry a real docker client --\n    that is exactly why this must be proven by construction, not assumed).\n\n    Task 026 (E.4), at the unit level the CLI reads through: with that\n    constructed PATH in force and `DOCKER` left at the CLI's own bare\n    default, the liveness probe answers `unknown` -- it could not decide --\n    rather than `absent`, which is docker's own answer about a container it\n    looked for and did not find.\n\n    Task 069's nightly re-take found the precondition below asserting\n    against an environment that never carries docker in the first place:\n    `.github/workflows/nightly.yml`'s dev-layout cells deliberately install\n    no docker client at all (`-m docker` coverage stays in `heavy.yml`), so\n    \"this dev container is expected to carry a real docker client\" is false\n    there by that workflow's own design, not by accident. Skipping rather\n    than failing keeps the precondition's job -- catching an accidental\n    ambient-docker pass on a host that DOES carry one -- without turning a\n    docker-less environment's absence of anything to remove into a defect.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Precondition proof, isolated from the CLI: the helper this module<br />\nrelies on for every other test here really does remove docker, using<br />\nthis host's own ambient PATH (which does carry a real docker client --<br />\nthat is exactly why this must be proven by construction, not assumed).</p>\n<pre><code>Task 026 (E.4), at the unit level the CLI reads through: with that\nconstructed PATH in force and `DOCKER` left at the CLI's own bare\ndefault, the liveness probe answers `unknown` -- it could not decide --\nrather than `absent`, which is docker's own answer about a container it\nlooked for and did not find.\n\nTask 069's nightly re-take found the precondition below asserting\nagainst an environment that never carries docker in the first place:\n`.github/workflows/nightly.yml`'s dev-layout cells deliberately install\nno docker client at all (`-m docker` coverage stays in `heavy.yml`), so\n&quot;this dev container is expected to carry a real docker client&quot; is false\nthere by that workflow's own design, not by accident. Skipping rather\nthan failing keeps the precondition's job -- catching an accidental\nambient-docker pass on a host that DOES carry one -- without turning a\ndocker-less environment's absence of anything to remove into a defect.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"skipped","statusMessage":"Skipped: no ambient docker client in this environment (expected on a nightly dev-layout cell, which installs none by design) -- nothing here for the removal below to exercise","statusTrace":"('/__w/ralphd/ralphd/tests/test_status_docker_removed_from_path_task026.py', 94, 'Skipped: no ambient docker client in this environment (expected on a nightly dev-layout cell, which installs none by design) -- nothing here for the removal below to exercise')","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791866910559,"stop":1791866910559,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791866910560,"stop":1791866910560,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"para